1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,080
The asteroid wiped out T. rex.
小行星灭了霸王龙。

2
00:00:02,080 --> 00:00:04,290
The crocodile basically just moved.
鳄鱼呢，基本上只是搬了个家。

3
00:00:04,290 --> 00:00:07,600
Sixty six million years ago, a rock ten kilometers wide
六千六百万年前，一块十公里宽的石头

4
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:08,930
slammed into Mexico.
砸进了墨西哥。

5
00:00:08,930 --> 00:00:11,280
About three quarters of all species vanished,
大约四分之三的物种消失了，

6
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:13,700
including every dinosaur that could not fly.
包括所有不会飞的恐龙。

7
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:14,950
But crocodiles made it.
可鳄鱼挺过来了。

8
00:00:14,950 --> 00:00:16,870
Their family is still here today.
它们的家族今天还在。

9
00:00:16,870 --> 00:00:18,750
And their family used to be wild:
它们当年可野了：

10
00:00:18,750 --> 00:00:21,930
armored plant eaters, land hunters, giants over a ton.
披甲的素食者、陆地猎手、一吨多重的巨兽。

11
00:00:21,930 --> 00:00:23,160
One called Sarcosuchus
有一种叫帝鳄，

12
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:25,280
could grow up to twelve meters long.
能长到十二米长。

13
00:00:25,280 --> 00:00:26,420
Today's brain teaser:
今天的烧脑问题：

14
00:00:26,420 --> 00:00:29,080
how does a cold blooded reptile outlive T. rex?
一只冷血爬行动物，凭什么活过霸王龙？

15
00:00:29,080 --> 00:00:31,380
A new study led by University College London
伦敦大学学院牵头的一项新研究，

16
00:00:31,380 --> 00:00:32,960
went looking for the answer.
专门去找答案。

17
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:36,060
They dug through more than seven thousand fossils and records
他们翻了七千多条化石和记录，

18
00:00:36,060 --> 00:00:37,750
from over four hundred species.
覆盖四百多个物种。

19
00:00:37,750 --> 00:00:39,250
Then they used climate models
再用气候模型，

20
00:00:39,250 --> 00:00:42,440
to rebuild two hundred forty five million years of weather.
重建了两亿四千五百万年的气候。

21
00:00:42,440 --> 00:00:44,090
Their finding, in one sentence:
结论一句话：

22
00:00:44,090 --> 00:00:45,650
crocodiles follow the heat.
鳄鱼追着热走。

23
00:00:45,650 --> 00:00:48,110
Think of a croc as a solar powered robot.
把鳄鱼想成一台太阳能机器人：

24
00:00:48,110 --> 00:00:49,250
No sun, no power.
没太阳，就没电。

25
00:00:49,250 --> 00:00:50,180
When Earth got hot,
地球一热，

26
00:00:50,180 --> 00:00:52,470
crocodile relatives spread toward the poles.
鳄鱼的亲戚就往两极扩张。

27
00:00:52,470 --> 00:00:55,780
Fifty million years ago, Earth was about ten degrees warmer.
五千万年前，地球比现在热大约十度，

28
00:00:55,780 --> 00:00:58,110
Crocodile relatives lived in Antarctica.
南极洲都有鳄鱼的亲戚。

29
00:00:58,110 --> 00:00:59,050
When Earth cooled,
地球一冷，

30
00:00:59,050 --> 00:01:00,740
they retreated to the tropics.
它们就退回热带。

31
00:01:00,740 --> 00:01:03,650
Twist one: mostly, they did not change to fit the climate.
反转一：它们多半不是改变自己去适应，

32
00:01:03,650 --> 00:01:04,820
They changed address.
而是换个地址。

33
00:01:04,820 --> 00:01:07,210
Scientists call it climatic niche conservatism.
科学家管这叫气候生态位保守。

34
00:01:07,210 --> 00:01:09,670
I call it never leaving your favorite blanket.
我管这叫：永远不离开最爱的那条毯子。

35
00:01:09,670 --> 00:01:10,530
Now, the asteroid.
现在说小行星。

36
00:01:10,530 --> 00:01:12,330
Dust and soot blocked the sunlight.
尘埃和烟灰挡住了阳光。

37
00:01:12,330 --> 00:01:13,480
The planet got darker
地球变暗，

38
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:14,200
and colder.
也变冷了。

39
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:15,510
The team ran simulations
团队做了模拟：

40
00:01:15,510 --> 00:01:17,750
with five or ten percent less sunlight.
阳光少百分之五，或者少百分之十。

41
00:01:17,750 --> 00:01:19,780
Near the equator, it stayed warm enough
赤道附近，仍然暖和到

42
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:20,690
for crocodiles.
鳄鱼能活。

43
00:01:20,690 --> 00:01:22,040
Twist two, the sneaky one:
反转二，最狡猾：

44
00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:24,100
they were already in the right place.
它们本来就站在对的位置。

45
00:01:24,100 --> 00:01:27,700
As the lead author puts it, the asteroid did not make the whole planet
第一作者说，小行星并没有让整个地球

46
00:01:27,700 --> 00:01:29,260
equally hostile to everyone.
对每个物种都一样凶。

47
00:01:29,260 --> 00:01:31,080
The team's earlier modeling showed
团队之前的模拟显示，

48
00:01:31,080 --> 00:01:33,030
dinosaur habitats shrank far more.
恐龙的栖息地缩得多得多。

49
00:01:33,030 --> 00:01:35,000
Only with fifteen percent less sunlight
只有阳光少到百分之十五，

50
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:36,690
would the tropical refuge fail.
热带避难所才会失守。

51
00:01:36,690 --> 00:01:38,670
The researchers think that extreme case
研究者认为，

52
00:01:38,670 --> 00:01:39,400
is unlikely.
那种极端情况不太可能。

53
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:40,850
Crocs had other tricks too:
鳄鱼还有别的招：

54
00:01:40,850 --> 00:01:44,460
small bodies, a life half in water, and they eat almost anything.
个头小，半泡在水里，什么都吃。

55
00:01:44,460 --> 00:01:46,310
Being cold blooded helped as well.
冷血也帮了忙：

56
00:01:46,310 --> 00:01:48,930
Low energy needs, so they can wait out hunger.
耗能低，饿得起。

57
00:01:48,930 --> 00:01:51,770
In a dark world, a hungry T. rex was in big trouble.
黑暗的世界里，饿肚子的霸王龙麻烦大了。

58
00:01:51,770 --> 00:01:52,880
A croc could wait.
鳄鱼可以等。

59
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:54,710
Twist three, and it is about today:
反转三，跟今天有关：

60
00:01:54,710 --> 00:01:57,080
crocodiles handle climate change by moving.
鳄鱼应对气候变化，靠的是搬家。

61
00:01:57,080 --> 00:01:59,300
But now there are roads, farms and cities
可现在，路、农田和城市

62
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:00,010
in the way.
挡在路上。

63
00:02:00,010 --> 00:02:01,820
The team says crocodiles need room
团队说，鳄鱼需要

64
00:02:01,820 --> 00:02:02,370
to move.
能搬家的空间。

65
00:02:02,370 --> 00:02:04,940
Their ancestors walked all the way to Antarctica.
它们的祖先能走到南极洲，

66
00:02:04,940 --> 00:02:07,220
Today's crocs can barely cross a highway.
今天的鳄鱼却连一条高速都过不去。

67
00:02:07,220 --> 00:02:09,430
The lesson of two hundred million years:
两亿多年的教训：

68
00:02:09,430 --> 00:02:12,270
sometimes survival just means being able to move.
活下来，有时候就是能搬家。

69
00:02:12,270 --> 00:02:14,550
Fine print: this is a model of the deep past,
友情提示：这是对远古的模型，

70
00:02:14,550 --> 00:02:16,940
pieced together from fossils and simulations.
靠化石和模拟拼出来的。

71
00:02:16,940 --> 00:02:18,420
Body size, diet and water
个头、食性、水，

72
00:02:18,420 --> 00:02:20,370
mattered too, not just climate.
也都很重要，不只是气候。

73
00:02:20,370 --> 00:02:22,280
So how did crocodiles outlive T. rex?
所以，鳄鱼凭什么活过霸王龙？

74
00:02:22,280 --> 00:02:24,830
They always had the seat closest to the heater.
它一直坐在离暖气最近的位置。

75
00:02:24,830 --> 00:02:27,070
The asteroid ended the age of dinosaurs.
小行星终结了恐龙时代。

76
00:02:27,070 --> 00:02:29,720
The crocodile just never left the heater.
鳄鱼呢，只是没离开暖气。

